<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>Tempest</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>Tempest.Blazor</PackageId>
    <Version>1.0.0-beta.4</Version>
    <Description>Component-owned state for Blazor. Three attributes and a bus.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
beta.4:
- Split into Tempest.Core (the [Command]/[Reactive]/[Event] attributes, the IEventBus contract, the CommandState/ReactiveState families and the ITempestComponent host contract) and Tempest.Blazor (StatefulComponent bases, EventBus, DI). Tempest.Blazor depends on Tempest.Core; the Tempest namespace is unchanged, so no code edits are needed.

beta.3:
- Generated state properties now match the accessibility of the member they wrap, so members typed with private nested types no longer hit CS0053. [Reactive] fields may now be any non-public accessibility.
- Generated files carry the source .razor file's @using directives plus all _Imports.razor usings, so field/return types that rely on a using (e.g. MudBlazor's DateRange) no longer hit CS0246.
- New StatefulLayoutComponent base for layouts (LayoutComponentBase flavor of StatefulComponent); state classes now take the ITempestComponent interface.

beta.2 (breaking): flat generated members (IsLoading{Name}, {Name}Error, {Name}Command, Try{Name}Command) are replaced by one {Name}State property per member.
- [Command] generates CommandState (Task/ValueTask/void) or CommandState&lt;T&gt; with Result/HasResult (Task&lt;T&gt;/ValueTask&lt;T&gt;/T).
- [Event, Command] generates EventCommandState&lt;TEvent&gt;.
- Latest-wins cancellation via an optional trailing CancellationToken parameter.
- New [Reactive] fields generate a ReactiveState&lt;T&gt; twin (Value/SetSilently/Initial/IsDirty/Reset) with an optional partial On{Name}Changed(T value) hook.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>andresitomanuel</Authors>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageOutputPath>..\..\artifacts</PackageOutputPath>
    <PackageTags>blazor;state;state-management;source-generator;events</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Tempest.Core\Tempest.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Ship the source generator inside the NuGet package -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Tempest.Generators\Tempest.Generators.csproj"
                      ReferenceOutputAssembly="false"
                      OutputItemType="Analyzer" />
    <None Include="..\Tempest.Generators\bin\$(Configuration)\netstandard2.0\Tempest.Generators.dll"
          Pack="true" PackagePath="analyzers/dotnet/cs" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
